{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: implement the adopted trusted-process/single-operator supported-host posture on current main afa911ea. This is the one current-world implementation assignment authorized by coordination request 9d9f3162 under planner promise 51f0f779, issued after both gate lanes sealed: fan-out e1ab6474 landed at 12105a30 and one-base-append 95f50368 landed at 44b54074 (main since advanced through the UI simplification a81d9c4a, its citation cleanups, and the onboarding-identity core afa911ea, whose landed behavior governs). Historical evidence, named and not rested on: adopted decision 8a758fb7, Hugh adoption bc758b7a, Claude independent approval 05c1062c with review ratification f8542488, design completion 2ff780f2, and every residual implementation finding from that review. This child deliberately does not rest on historical self-request 3fec5026 (#2544), the coordination chain, or any retired or world-stale record, so that retiring #2544 cannot stale this assignment. Path scope: internal/service, internal/app, cmd/gitseq-mcp, internal/residentclient, ui, docs — the exact live artifacts at those six paths are this request's only bases.","body":{"conditions":"1. Operator acknowledgement: enforce the trusted-process/single-operator posture without building partial shared-host authentication. Choose and name one deliberate per-invocation or explicit named-config operator acknowledgement; fail closed when it is absent; document that it discloses the boundary but does not protect direct gs CLI key access or same-account malware. Resolve every configured listener address and require every result to be loopback; refuse non-loopback. Preserve and test the pre-side-effect Origin, Host, and content-type policy with no permissive CORS path.\n2. Credentials: replace client-chosen bearer identifiers with resident-minted credentials using at least 128 bits from system cryptographic randomness and a validated opaque form. Bind each credential to exactly one repository and actor; keep the public handle display-only; prevent cross-actor/cross-repository use and replay after departure, non-renewed expiry, restart, or explicit revocation. Preserve the existing global/per-actor session caps, TTL bound, recycled-identifier inbox cleanup, and route-template-only telemetry unless stronger evidence justifies a reviewed change.\n3. Disclosure removal: remove credential disclosure from presence and ordinary status, MCP whoami/tool results, logs, diagnostics, durable events, referrers, query strings, path segments, returned URL errors, and browser/MCP departure flows, covering both browser UI and MCP clients. Add adversarial tests for guessing, theft/replay, cross-actor and cross-repository confusion, renewal, departure, expiry/restart/revocation, hostile browser origins, malformed credentials, and diagnostics; state plainly that malicious same-account processes remain out of scope.\n4. Documentation in the same exact implementation head: update startup output, resident status, browser guidance, MCP guidance, deployment/security documentation, and docs/reference/architecture.md. Document the OS account, repository common directory, backups, snapshots, developer tooling, sync/copy paths, compromise response, key/capability recovery and rotation boundary; correct the inaccurate internal/custody key-management row; name architecture layers 3 and 7 plus internal/app, and state that kernel verification and fold semantics do not change.\n5. Process: implement on a request/\u003cslug\u003e branch with Rests-On naming this request; publish the normal exact-head artifact report at every maintained path the head changes, and obtain an independent Architecture/Security/Simplification implementation review before merge, including a simplification check that rejects a partial authentication framework which cannot protect against same-account peers.","priority":"P1","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}